invariant: INV-43
file: p256_wide_verify_point.c
catches: test/wycheproof.sh
reason: the host verifier compares R's affine x with r and never with
  r + n, so it refuses a signature whose R has an x of n or more. x is
  below p and r is below n, so the two differ only for an x of n or more,
  which is one point in 2^128: no random signature shows it. Wycheproof's
  ECDSA vectors hold signatures whose k*G has such an x, and its host test
  runs them on this file.

--- old
    if ((uint64_t)(sum_limb >> 64) != 0 || p256_wide_fe_reduced_mask(&c) == 0) {
        return 0;
    }
    return x_is(sum, &zz, &c);
--- new
    return 0;
